WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
Descent and restoration echo through dreams, garments, concealment and recognition. Follow the site’s proposed narrative map.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:15.000
9 thematic movements in this study arrangement. The labels summarize passages; they are not Quran translations.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:25.000
The prologue introduces the account as revealed narrative. The epilogue asks readers to draw a lesson from the stories. Together they frame the telling.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Joseph’s dream at the beginning is explicitly recalled at its fulfilment. This is a direct narrative correspondence.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:45.000
A garment first supports deception and grief; later Joseph’s shirt becomes an instrument of restoration. Read how the same motif changes its role.

00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.000
Joseph enters Egypt vulnerable and accused. Later his brothers encounter him in a position

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:55.000
of authority. The narrative reverses roles while raising questions of truth and justice.

00:00:55.000 --> 00:01:04.000
The selected hinge, 12:36–57, moves through prison, interpretation, vindication and appointment. In this map the direction of Joseph’s circumstances changes.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:11.000
The connecting marks gather into nested rings. Their symmetry visualizes this reading; it does not establish the reading by itself.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:20.000
Read the opening dream beside 12:100. Which correspondences are explicit in the narrative, and which are interpretive?
